schema: test/v2
level: working-unit
epic: E-GATETRUTH
wu: E-GATETRUTH.W4
branch: wu/gate-truth/link-integrity
tests:
  unit:
    count: 9
    covers: "doc.rs: link_targets over every href shape the corpus carries, asserting only relative file targets survive - a bare fragment, an empty href, http/https, mailto, a root-relative path and both .archive spellings are dropped, and a fragment is stripped off a target that is kept; an href inside a <script> or <style> body is data, not a link (the raw-text rule the tokeniser already owns, so the case is pinned rather than newly handled). check_links against real tempdir trees: a resolving target yields nothing, a missing one yields exactly one Failure whose `what` carries the href verbatim and whose `fix` names both repairs; one dead target linked twice is one failure; resolution is against the DOC's directory, not the repo root - a doc in decisions/ reaches ../workflow.html and does not reach workflow.html. with_links scope: an ungoverned doc goes red while still matching Verdict::Ungoverned, so the identity survives the failure and the verdict cannot claim a checklist ran; a draft is silent on a dead link and an archived-but-shipped doc is not; a doc living under .archive is not checked at all; a governed doc reports its checklist failures and its link failure together."
  integration:
    count: 7
    covers: "tests/verify_doc.rs, driving the built xtask binary over temp trees: an ungoverned doc with a dead href exits 1 and names the href - the DEC-13 shape, and the assertion that reds against the parent commit; the same doc with the target present exits 0 and still prints `ungoverned`; a governed doc missing an item AND carrying a dead href prints both, proving the predicate composes rather than short-circuits; a draft with the same dead href exits 0; a link into .archive/ and a doc living under .archive/ are both green in one run; https, a bare fragment and mailto are green. Plus the epic e2e's step 3 as a corpus run: git ls-files over this repo's own docs/ through the binary, asserting exit 0, so expected result 5 is a test rather than a claim."
  e2e:
    count: 0
    waived: "The epic's e2e is one gated WU merge on a synthetic repo proving all four fixes compose, and it is owed at the epic close - W1, W2 and W3 each deferred their steps the same way. This WU's share of it is step 3 (run verify-doc over that repo's docs, one link deliberately dead; red naming the href, green once fixed), which ships above as the integration row on the same hermetic temp-tree shape the epic step will reuse. Nothing about this WU's requirement needs a gated merge to observe."
note: "E-GATETRUTH.W4 fixes P2b: nothing checked whether a doc's links resolved. The fix that mattered was not reading hrefs but reading them on docs verify-doc had never opened - verify_html_against returns Ungoverned the moment a doc declares no data-artifact, before any predicate runs, and all four dead links E-DFLOW.W12 found by hand sat in exactly those docs (c5f474b says so outright; DEC-13 is the permanent T2 record among them). So the predicate runs beside the artifact read rather than behind it, and Verdict::Ungoverned and Verdict::Exempt each gained a failures list so a doc can be red while still reporting what it is. Counts above are the diff's added #[test] functions at this tip, 16 in all. Regression proof, run at c575ab9 by restoring doc.rs from 4bc7146: 2 FAILED, 14 passed - exactly the two asserting the new behaviour (an_ungoverned_doc_with_a_dead_link_is_red, a_governed_doc_reports_the_dead_link_beside_its_checklist_failures); the other fourteen assert unchanged behaviour and pass on both sides, so they are pinned rather than tautological. The DEC-13 defect was additionally reproduced by hand against the shipped code - its href reverted to the setup.ts it shipped with - and reds, naming the href; the file was restored. cargo test --workspace green, 414 in all (xtask lib 236, mr 58, verify_doc 16, doc_hooks 8, gate0_cache 5, ui 2; root package trawler 65, api 11, e2e_capture 6, e2e_h2 4, ca 3); cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features -D warnings clean; cargo fmt --check clean. cargo xtask verify-doc over every tracked doc: 44 checked, none red."
